+
+## Companion Objects and Module-Level Function Translation
+
+Python modules frequently expose free functions alongside classes. In Scala 2.13, map these to companion objects or utility `object`s while preserving the expected API names.
+
+```python
+# Python module
+class Token:
+    def __init__(self, text):
+        self.text = text
+
+
+def to_token(text):
+    return Token(text)
+
+
+def tokenize_batch(values):
+    return [to_token(v) for v in values]
+```
+
+```scala
+final case class Token(text: String)
+
+object Token {
+  def toToken(text: String): Token = Token(text)
+
+  def tokenizeBatch(values: Seq[String]): Seq[Token] =
+    values.map(toToken)
+}
+```
+
+Prefer simple companion objects and utility objects over introducing service layers or extra wrapper types.
+
+For sealed ADTs translated from Python enums/constants, keep the hierarchy compact and evaluator-friendly:
+
+```scala
+sealed trait TokenType extends Product with Serializable
+
+object TokenType {
+  case object StringToken extends TokenType
+  case object NumericToken extends TokenType
+  case object TemporalToken extends TokenType
+}
+```
+
+Use exhaustive pattern matching, but avoid expanding the domain model beyond the original Python semantics.
 
